# Per-project state never belongs in the tool repo.
#
# etc/ holds the generated SSH private key and the SSH/RDP identities;
# .run/ holds pidfiles and daemon logs; captures/ holds raw traces, which are
# both large and potentially device-serial-identifying.
etc/
.run/
captures/

# A project scaffolded inside a clone ('harness init .') would otherwise drag
# its state and its generated media in with it.
/harness.conf
bootstrap.iso
*.pcapng
*.pcap

# ...but the example configurations are documentation and belong in the repo.
!examples/*/harness.conf
!examples/*/hwdbg.conf
